{"name":"Org-Nouveau","title":"Org-Nouveau","revision":236710,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Org-Nouveau","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Org-Nouveau is a visual art-inspired style prevalent in the late 1980s to 1990s. It is centered on fluent natural lines, organic architecture, and a revival of early-20th-century Art Nouveau and Catalan Modernisme. It features growing, wet, or skeletal natural forms, whiplash, sinuous lines and asymmetrical \"S\" curves, replicating vines, tendrils, and stems."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The main focus of this visual aesthetic includes stones, fluid stairwells, ironwork and grotto-based elements, coral-like structures, watery, under-the-sea iridescence, melting, cavernous plaster forms, carved wood, wrought iron, stone, and stained glass shaped to look fluid or alive."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Prehistoric-inspired interior design"},{"kind":"list","text":"Microorganism designs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Caves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kitschy Woods"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shells"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bones"},{"kind":"list","text":"Blobby furniture"},{"kind":"list","text":"Corals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stones"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Brands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Starbucks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Olive Garden"},{"kind":"list","text":"Di Petsa"},{"kind":"list","text":"Collina Strada"},{"kind":"list","text":"Iris Van Herpen"},{"kind":"list","text":"Y/Project"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ayllón"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mondo Mondo"},{"kind":"list","text":"Alan Crocetti"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hugo Kreit"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gaetano Pesce"},{"kind":"list","text":"Entler"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Locations"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Nautilus House (Mexico"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jordan Mozer Designs (Chicago, USA)"},{"kind":"lis